Hello all!

After a few false starts I am doing well with a Samurai.  Things
started out well, I found an altar on level one!  But there weren't
enough enemies around to get an artifact and he was getting hungry.  I
grabbed some levels in the first level of the Mines and in the second
level I found not one but TWO bones levels by the stairs!  Weird!

Apparently a Tourist and Wizard were killed by the same giant beetle
mere spaces from each other.  I got a cloak of magic resistance and
lots of UnID'ed stuff.  The altar said it was all cursed so I shoved it
in a chest and moved on.

I headed for Sobokan, and somewhere along the way I found a bag of
holding!  Nice!  Now if I can get an amulet of reflection I'd be set
for awhile.  I didn't find a single store along the way.  Meh.

In Sobokan, I got an amulet of reflection.  The yumi came in handy
here.  3 times there was a giant mimic in a spot I needed to go and I
was able to kill it with arrows and not damage my luck.

I headed to mine town and found, to my dismay, that it was dark and
full of peaceful dwarves with pickaxes.  I killed them anway, because I
like my levels neat and tidy, and those dwarves just dig everything up.

I made a new STASH in the non-aligned temple, donated for 4 AC and
found that my lamp was magic!  Sweet!  Except this character is
supposed to be wishless, genoless, and polyless....

I price ID'ed everything I had and found yet another bag of holding!
And the light shop was full of candles.  That's good, because my wizard
had to wish for candles to finish the game.

I decided that the cloak of magic resistance was too important, even
cursed, and put it on over some decent armor.  It was +0, so I figured
if I prayed on the altar on D1 it would uncurse.  Nope, God is
displeased!  Guess I didn't wait long enough.  There weren't any
monsters around for me to sac, so I just tried it.

So I went into the mines and it is a good thing I had the MR.  I
stepped on a lot of poly traps and would've broke my poly conduct
otherwise.  Got the luckstone and ID'ed it.

I think at this point I got holy water and uncursed the cloak and
blessed the BoH, uni horn, and luckstone.  Things are really looking up
at this point.

I plunge into the dungeon and do my best to make it to Medusa as fast
as possible, just so I know where she is level-wise.  Along the way I
find 3 more altars and convert them.  I find zero shops and zero
temples.  I have to go to minetown donate.  Before I go back, I clear
out 2 leprechuan halls and end up going back with $30k in gold.  I
easily get to AC 1 naked, and leave the rest in te general store.  I
actually have to buy some junk at the gen store so I can continue to
price ID items.

I eat some giants and get my strength up to 18/40ish.  My Int, Wis, and
Cha are still really low so spell casting and foobus dancing are out of
the question.  I nurse dance a bit and kill a couple of nurses too.
I'm really impatient with nurses.  If there are monsters around I am
more likely to kill them just to get them off my back.  That's is
probably why my characters usually only have 300 something hp.  One of
these days I break 1000 hp.  Maybe this game if I can find the
patience.

I don't bother looking for vaults but I finish exploring each level
before Medusa and find 2 more magic lamps.  It's tempting, but I'm
doing ok so I don't use the wishes.

For awhile I'm stuck at XL 13 and I ultimately resort to lots of creat
monster scrolls to get a level.  My attempts at wraith baiting before
that net me a corpse but it rots away.

Finally at XL 14, I tackled the quest.  I remember reading that the
samurai quest is difficult but not as bad as the monk quest.  I'm glad
I have reflection when a Joshu zaps a wand of death at me.  For that
matter, I'm glad I have reflection against all those wands.  When I get
to the bottom level I accidently munch on a samurai corpse instead of a
cream pie.  I'll need to get to XL 15 to get stealth to counteract that
aggravate monster.

I wake the nemesis prematurely when I'm breaking wands trying to
unburden myself and keep those wands away from monsters.  He comes over
and hits me twice.  I live.  I run away.  I continue trying to unburden
myself, and he comes over and hits me again.  Twice.  I survive intact.
 Phew!  Then I remember the wand of death.  It turns out he doesn't
have reflection so that is good for me.

I take the Tsugriooogie (yeah that word) and boogie back to my stash.
By the way, does the quest area keep generating ninjas?  That would be
a great source of potions of paralysis and confusion.

I dump Snickersnee for the quest item.  Oh, I forgot to mention I
sac'ed for Snickersnee, Firebrand, and Sun Sword.  I found Snickersnee
to be the most useful of those, but the quest reward out damages it big
time.

I get to Medusas and still have no levitation.  I get my first set of
dragon scales and they are yellow.  Blah.  And I discovered that
hitting an ochre jelly can corrode my +3 helmet for some strange
reason. I thought I was only risking my sword, which is apparent
rustproof.

I have a cursed potion of gain level so I zap a hole in the floor.  At
the castle I wake up everything with aggravate monster.  I figure out
the pass tune and crush a lot of Liches, Disenchanters, Trolls, and
Soldiers.  I do manage to get a wand of death and a potion of full
healing from all that.

I almost drown when I miskey and step into water instead of on the
drawbridge.  But I'm really lucky.  The end results of that misstep
are: 1. my key rusts.  2. My corroded helmet rusts.  3.  My potion of
fruit juice dilutes.  Minor stuff.

I get the WoW and don't use it.  I kill as silver dragon but no scales.
 Also, not magic marker or scrolls of enchant armor.  I find three
pairs good boots. One pair turns out to be speed.  One is fumbling.
Don't know what the third is yet, but it is cursed.

So that is where I am now.  Oh, and I put on an amulet and change and
become a woman.

I'm still genoless, wishless (although SDSM is tempting me), and
polyless.  Haven't changed form, haven't polyed any monsters or items.
I'm pretty sure one of the 200 potions in my stash is polymorph so I
will have to ID those to be sure before drinking.



